SUSFS 2.3.0 integration tests
============================

From the kernel root:

    python3 tools/testing/selftests/susfs/test_integration.py
    python3 tools/testing/selftests/susfs/test_integration.py --config out/.config
    python3 tools/testing/selftests/susfs/test_integration.py --host-tests --cc clang
    python3 tools/testing/selftests/susfs/test_integration.py --host-tests \
        --cc 'clang -fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all'

Integrity-only checks require standard-library Python, no network or compiler.
They verify pinned source/hook postimages, single wiring, platform dependencies
and the requested full feature profile. CI runs them after olddefconfig.

--profile disabled checks all SUSFS settings are off; --profile minimal expects
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS=y with all subfeatures off. Use --config with those output files.
Run KSU and NoMount selftests separately for their source/config policies.

--host-tests extracts the current reboot dispatcher, original setuid handler,
augmented unmount path, UID helpers, flag predicates, readlink helper, pagemap
zero-entry helper and mount-ID release function. It runs single-threaded mocks:
256 authorization, 1792 credential/unmount, 3010 readlink/hash/fault and 2404
pagemap cases, plus flag/ID checks. No actual rules or kernel operations occur.

--negative choices no-auth, no-zygote-guard, readlink-zero-count, hash-collision,
free-borrowed-id deliberately change extracted code IN MEMORY, then must compile
and fail a runtime assertion. A nonzero exit is expected, and source is unchanged.

Models do not establish real VFS/RCU/fsnotify/mmap/superblock behavior, concurrent
safety, working Android root/modules, a full kernel build, boot or integrity-check
results. See Documentation/filesystems/susfs/integration.md for limitations and
device testing. Do not regenerate provenance merely to bypass failed tests.

BPF/task-header provenance follow-up
----------------------------------
The immutable original SUSFS manifest is still checked. Later approved task
header changes use Documentation/bpf/susfs-compat-overlay.json and its exact
reviewed patch; only include/linux/sched.h is allowed in that chain. All
other hooks, including the existing FinaSU overlay, remain fail-closed.

Run the positive/13-negative provenance regression with:
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/susfs/test_provenance_overlays.py --config out/.config
The CI build script runs this check before compilation.
